## Clean up resources

After completing the lab, delete your assets in the order shown below. The deletion order is designed to delete dependent assets before the assets they depend on.

!!! warning "Delete only your own assets"
    In a shared workspace, delete only the assets with `<your_name>` in their names.

{% if N.mcp %}
1. **MCP connections:** In your terminal, run `ug mcp remove` and select the Genie connections you added in Step {{ N.mcp }}. If you added them with `claude mcp add`, run `claude mcp remove genie-one` instead. The MCP servers themselves stay in the workspace.

{% endif %}
1. **Genie Agent:** Open `<your_name> - {{ s.naming.agent }}` in **Genie Agents**, click the kebab menu (⋮) in the top-right corner, and select **Move to trash**.

    {{ shot('99-wrap-up/99-01-delete-genie-agent.png', 'Delete Genie Agent') }}

{% if N.dash %}
2. **Dashboard:** Open `<your_name> - {{ s.naming.dashboard }}` in **Dashboards**, click the kebab menu (⋮) in the top-right corner, select **File actions** → **Move to trash**.

    {{ shot('99-wrap-up/99-02-delete-dashboard.png', 'Delete dashboard') }}
{% endif %}

3. **Page:** Go to **Discover** → **Pages** and open each of {{ s.improve.pages | map(attribute='name') | map('code') | oxford }} Pages, then click the kebab menu (⋮) → **Delete**.

    {{ shot('99-wrap-up/99-03-delete-page.png', 'Delete Page') }}

4. **Domain:** Open the `{{ cat }}` Domain in **Discover**, click **Edit** → **Remove domain**.

    {{ shot('99-wrap-up/99-04-delete-domain.png', 'Delete Domain') }}

5. **Governed Tag:** Search for `{{ cat }}` in **Catalog** → **Govern** → **Governed Tags**, open it, and click **Delete** in the top-right corner.

    {{ shot('99-wrap-up/99-05-delete-governed-tag.png', 'Delete Governed Tag') }}

6. **Pipeline:** Click the kebab menu (⋮) next to `<your_name>_{{ s.naming.pipeline }}` in **Jobs & Pipelines** and select **Delete**.

    {{ shot('99-wrap-up/99-06-delete-pipeline.png', 'Delete pipeline') }}

7. **Catalog:** Open `{{ cat }}` in **Catalog**, click the kebab menu (⋮) to the right of the catalog name, and select **Delete**. All tables{{ ', Metric Views, and Volumes' if s.options.volumes else ' and Metric Views' }} in the catalog will be deleted together.

    {{ shot('99-wrap-up/99-07-delete-catalog.png', 'Delete catalog') }}

??? tip "Delete catalog with SQL"
    You can also delete the catalog and all assets inside it by running the following query in SQL Editor. Confirm the catalog name carefully: deletion cannot be undone.

    ```sql
    DROP CATALOG {{ cat }} CASCADE;
    ```

